# HG2-A (group B; values by the norm): `x := 2` is the local of the call (#call-frame-20261115: no write-back), so work\data\x stays 1 after each call: published 1 (pinned 2), and the second call pairs 2 with 1: second 21 (pinned 22). first stays 21. Observation: the root values are written explicitly in sub: observe (#flush-receiver-contract; #call-frame-20261115).
(
    Observed:
        int: first 0
        int: published 0
        int: second 0
)
@: shared data[0]
# Evaluate both arguments before publishing x. Bare x and the explicit graph path differ on the first call.
fn: pair (int: a; int: b) int
    return: a * 10 + b
end: pair
fn: work () int (int: x 1; int: seen 0)
    x := 2
    seen := pair(x; work\data\x)
    return: seen
end: work
int: first work()
int: published work\data\x
int: second work()

sub: observe ()
    shared\Observed\first := first
    shared\Observed\published := published
    shared\Observed\second := second
observe()
